        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0467" n="397" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg397"/>

                <head>No. 210.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sargent to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 22, 1883</date>.
                        (Received November 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 205.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    last night of your telegram, reading as follows: [See <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, No. 207.] I have to-day communicated a copy of the above
                    telegram to Mr. W. O. Fox, consul at Brunswick, with instructions to carefully
                    and promptly execute it. I will send this report as soon as it is received. A
                    copy of my letter to him is herewith inclosed.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. A. SARGENT.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d210-a1.xml" xpointer="d210-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
